{"id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch10_SymmetricSpacesAndHolonomy#def:pet-ch10-tp-decomposition","title":"def:pet-ch10-tp-decomposition","path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch10_SymmetricSpacesAndHolonomy.md","line":113,"body":"","kind":"definition","status":"not_started","tex":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch10_SymmetricSpacesAndHolonomy.tex#def:pet-ch10-tp-decomposition","uses":["[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch10_SymmetricSpacesAndHolonomy#prop:pet-ch10-sigma-p-involution]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch10_SymmetricSpacesAndHolonomy.tex","label":"def:pet-ch10-tp-decomposition","line":265,"source":"\\begin{definition}[the subspaces $t_p$ and $s_p$]\n  \\label{def:pet-ch10-tp-decomposition}\n\n  \\source{petersen:page-0384}\n  \\uses{prop:pet-ch10-sigma-p-involution}\n  Let $t_p$ be the $(-1)$-eigenspace of $\\sigma_p$. Then\n  \\cref{prop:pet-ch10-sigma-p-involution} gives\n  \\[\n    t_p=\\{X\\in\\mathrm{iso}:(\\nabla X)_p=0\\},\\qquad\n    t_p\\xrightarrow{\\ X\\mapsto X_p\\ }T_pM\n  \\]\n  as a linear isomorphism. Hence $\\mathrm{iso}=t_p\\oplus\\mathrm{iso}_p$, and\n  \\[\n    \\mathrm{iso}\\simeq T_pM\\oplus s_p\\subset T_pM\\oplus\\mathfrak{so}(T_pM),\n    \\qquad\n    s_p=\\{(\\nabla X)|_p\\in\\mathfrak{so}(T_pM)\\mid X\\in\\mathrm{iso}_p\\}.\n  \\]\n\\end{definition}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Definition</div></section>[the subspaces <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$t_p$\">$t_p$</span> and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$s_p$\">$s_p$</span>] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6465663a7065742d636831302d74702d6465636f6d706f736974696f6e\"></span> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source\" style=\"display:block\">Source: <span class=\"reference\">petersen:page-0384</span></span> <a class=\"wikilink t